# Local Meshy review and intermediate exports; retain original reference and source GLB.
assets-src/dragonhead-*/dragonhead-form-review.blend*
assets-src/dragonhead-*/draft-hull.json
assets-src/dragonhead-*/ship-builder.mjs
assets-src/dragonhead-*/meshes/dragonhead-fitted-lod*.glb
assets-src/dragonhead-*/renders/
assets-src/dragonhead-*/props.provider-private.json
# Rejected title candidates stay local; the chosen source and the final PNG are tracked.
assets-src/menu-title-*/candidates*/
# Campaign camp models: rejected concept images and Meshy previews stay local, and so do the Meshy originals (about 5 MB
# each; provenance.json keeps their hashes and task ids). Chosen concepts are tracked.
assets-src/camps-meshy-*/candidates/
assets-src/camps-meshy-*/originals/
# Campaign map models (Meshy Smart Topology): the same, rejected concepts, previews and the Meshy originals stay local.
assets-src/map-models-*/candidates/
assets-src/map-models-*/originals/
.vite/
# Armor art: a raw replaced by a regeneration stays local (provenance.json keeps every request and why it was redone).
assets-src/armor-*/rejected/
# General figures cast pipeline: concept sheets, Meshy originals, rigs and motions (about 7.6 GB) stay local, since CI
# pulls every tracked binary; the json records beside them keep their prompts, task ids and hashes.
assets-src/generals-cast-2026-10-17/**/*.png
assets-src/generals-cast-2026-10-17/**/*.jpg
assets-src/generals-cast-2026-10-17/**/*.glb
